      en: "Cumura is a settlement of outstanding social and humanitarian significance, located on the outskirts of Bissau. The site gained international recognition due to its leprosarium and the missionary work of the Franciscan Order, which has been active here since the mid-20th century. Cumura is far more than a mere medical center; it is a community dedicated to the care and social integration of individuals with chronic illnesses. The town's architecture is dominated by the sprawling hospital complex, which, with its shaded corridors and functional wards, stands as a testament to the tradition of Christian charity in West Africa. Geographically, Cumura is situated in a water-rich zone near the Geba River, enabling the cultivation of vegetables and fruit for self-sufficiency. Over the decades, the settlement has evolved into a place of hope where education and preventive healthcare operate in tandem. Beside the hospital, Cumura houses schools and social facilities open to children from throughout the region. The town maintains a peaceful and orderly atmosphere that contrasts sharply with the hectic dynamics of the nearby capital. For Guinea-Bissau, Cumura is a symbol of solidarity and tireless dedication to the most vulnerable members of society."
